---
title: "Activate 4DA Signal"
description: "Open your 4DA Signal licence key in the app."
permalink: "/activate.html"
noAnalytics: true
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{#
  WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS
  --------------------
  The licence email used to link straight to a custom-scheme URL. Gmail strips
  custom-scheme hrefs outright -- in the browser and in its mobile apps -- so the
  button rendered but carried no href at all and did nothing when clicked.

  The scheme is `fourda`, not `4da`: a URL scheme must start with a letter
  (RFC 3986 / WHATWG), so browsers parsed `4da://...` as a RELATIVE path --
  "Open in 4DA" navigated to https://4da.ai/4da://activate?key=... and 404'd,
  leaking the key into the URL path besides. The OS registry happily registers
  digit-first scheme names, which is why the handler side always looked healthy
  while no browser could ever reach it. Renamed 2026-08-18 (app + this page +
  /signal/success together).

  So the email now links here over https, which every mail client permits, and this
  page performs the handoff to `fourda://` from a real user gesture on a real web
  page. That is the same bridge pattern Slack, Zoom and Figma use for desktop
  handoff.

  THE KEY TRAVELS IN THE FRAGMENT, NOT THE QUERY STRING.
  A fragment is never transmitted to the server, so the licence key stays out of
  Cloudflare's request logs and out of any Referer header sent to a third party.
  `noAnalytics: true` above additionally keeps PostHog off this page, because an
  analytics script can read `location.hash` even though the server cannot.
#}

{% block head %}
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://4da.ai/activate">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body {
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
      background: #0A0A0A; color: #FFFFFF; min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    }
    .card {
      background: #141414; border: 1px solid #2A2A2A; border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 40px; max-width: 480px; width: 100%; margin: 20px; text-align: center;
    }
    .mark { font-size: 40px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    h1 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .subtitle { font-size: 14px; color: #A0A0A0; margin-bottom: 28px; line-height: 1.5; }
    .license-key {
      display: block; padding: 12px; background: #0A0A0A; border: 1px solid #2A2A2A;
      border-radius: 6px; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px;
      color: #D4AF37; word-break: break-all; user-select: all; text-align: left;
    }
    .btn-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-top: 16px; }
    .btn-row button {
      flex: 1; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
      border: none; border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.2s;
    }
    .open-btn { background: #D4AF37; color: #0A0A0A; }
    .open-btn:hover { background: #C4A030; }
    .copy-btn { background: #1F1F1F; color: #A0A0A0; border: 1px solid #2A2A2A !important; }
    .copy-btn:hover { color: #fff; border-color: #D4AF37 !important; }
    .steps { margin-top: 24px; text-align: left; font-size: 13px; color: #A0A0A0; line-height: 1.8; }
    .steps strong { color: #fff; }
    .note { margin-top: 16px; padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 13px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.5; }
    .note.info { background: #D4AF3710; border: 1px solid #D4AF3730; color: #D4AF37; }
    .note.error { background: #EF444410; border: 1px solid #EF444430; color: #EF4444; }
    a { color: #D4AF37; text-decoration: none; }
    a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
  <div class="card">
    <div class="mark" id="mark">&#9679;</div>
    <h1 id="heading">Activate 4DA Signal</h1>
    <p class="subtitle" id="subtitle">Reading your licence key&hellip;</p>

    <div id="body-slot"></div>

    <div class="steps" id="steps" style="display:none;">
      <p><strong>If nothing opens:</strong></p>
      <p>1. Make sure 4DA is installed &mdash; <a href="/download">download it here</a></p>
      <p>2. Copy the key above, then in 4DA go to <strong>Settings &rarr; License</strong> and paste it</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;"><a href="/signal">Back to Signal</a> &middot; <a href="/">Home</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    // The key arrives in the fragment (#key=...), which the browser never sends to
    // the server. Support ?key= too, because a mail client that rewrites links may
    // convert the fragment -- but never advertise that form.
    function readKey() {
      var hash = window.location.hash || '';
      var m = hash.match(/(?:^#|&)key=([^&]+)/);
      if (m) return decodeURIComponent(m[1]);
      var q = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('key');
      return q || null;
    }

    function show(cls, text) {
      var el = document.createElement('div');
      el.className = 'note ' + cls;
      el.textContent = text;
      document.getElementById('body-slot').appendChild(el);
    }

    var key = readKey();

    if (!key || key.indexOf('4DA-') !== 0) {
      document.getElementById('mark').innerHTML = '&#33;';
      document.getElementById('heading').textContent = 'No licence key in this link';
      document.getElementById('subtitle').textContent =
        'Open the link straight from your licence email, or paste the key into 4DA by hand.';
      show('error', 'The activation link did not carry a key. This happens if the URL was truncated when it was copied.');
      document.getElementById('steps').style.display = 'block';
    } else {
      document.getElementById('heading').textContent = 'Your licence key';
      document.getElementById('subtitle').textContent =
        'Click below to hand it to 4DA. The app must already be installed.';

      var slot = document.getElementById('body-slot');
      var code = document.createElement('code');
      code.className = 'license-key';
      code.textContent = key;
      slot.appendChild(code);

      var row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'btn-row';
      var open = document.createElement('button');
      open.className = 'open-btn';
      open.textContent = 'Open in 4DA';
      var copy = document.createElement('button');
      copy.className = 'copy-btn';
      copy.textContent = 'Copy key';
      row.appendChild(open);
      row.appendChild(copy);
      slot.appendChild(row);

      document.getElementById('steps').style.display = 'block';

      open.addEventListener('click', function () {
        // Navigating to a custom scheme is allowed here because this is an ordinary
        // web page reacting to a click -- the restriction that broke the email
        // button is a mail-client sanitiser, not a browser policy.
        //
        // `fourda://`, never `4da://`: a URL scheme must start with a LETTER
        // (RFC 3986 / WHATWG). Browsers parse `4da://...` as a RELATIVE path, so
        // this exact line used to navigate to https://4da.ai/4da://activate?key=...
        // -- a 404 that also put the key in the server-visible URL. Verified
        // 2026-08-18; the app registers `fourda` (tauri.conf.json).
        window.location.href = 'fourda://activate?key=' + encodeURIComponent(key);
      });

      copy.addEventListener('click', function () {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(key).then(function () {
          copy.textContent = 'Copied';
          setTimeout(function () { copy.textContent = 'Copy key'; }, 2000);
        }, function () {
          show('error', 'Could not copy automatically — select the key above and copy it.');
        });
      });

      // Offer the deep link immediately; a browser that has the handler registered
      // will prompt, and one that does not simply stays on this page with the key
      // visible. Deliberately NOT automatic: an unprompted protocol navigation on
      // page load is what makes these pages feel broken when the app is absent.
    }
  </script>
{% endblock %}
